<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45786" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭb-audĭo</span></b> , ii,
			ītum, 4, v. n. (postclass.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To understand</i>, <i>supply</i> a
			word omitted: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subaudito jubeo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					28, 5, 1</span></i>
			; Aug. Civ. Dei, 15, 7; 17, 11; Greg. M. in Job, 33,
			17.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To hear a little</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nocturnis subaudiens vocibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 5, p. 167, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
